From 0321df696b8107f87f174fb2caebc06a0710c76d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:28:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HH-DATA: household data and rules, HOUS chunk, household cap
 20 everywhere

household.h/.c: residents' households (up to 24 records of 20), household 0's relation rows,
HREL_* with the pure reverse table, the section 3 rulebook with reason codes, join / leave / move /
head / reorder, household_new_person, the 'HOUS' save chunk (15th registry slot, nothing written
while empty). family_cap() is 20 on every platform and FAMILY_MAX 20 on the GBA too.
core/tests/test_household.c: 50 tests incl. a fuzz of the chunk. cross-stream: save.c skips the
empty HOUS header; family.c gets family_slot_move and one household_forget call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63cyoVQMX8CCuWDX8Db9
